      "before": "<p>(b) $\\|x-x_1\\|=\\sqrt{0.2^2+0.05^2}=0.206\\gt0.20$ and $\\|x-x_2\\|=\\sqrt{0.1^2+0.05^2}=0.112\\gt0.10$: neither ball contains $x$, so the condition triggers. Eq. 12 maximises $l_n(a_s)-L_x\\|x-x_s\\|$: backup 1 gives $0.5-2\\cdot0.206=0.088$, backup 2 gives $0.3-2\\cdot0.112=0.076$; select $a_1^*=a_1$. Both margins happen to be non-negative (Lemma A.6 guarantees this at least for the pair that certified the previous sample), and the larger one is the safer choice.</p>",
